  "biobricks:reviewed": false,
  "biobricks:reviewNotes": "Determined by the BioBricks licensing-annotation agent (slice items[498:504]). The brick harvests search results from OECD eChemPortal by scripting its substance-search UI and exporting CSVs. eChemPortal is a search/aggregation portal, not a data owner: it federates ~35 third-party regulatory databases, each with its own (and varying) terms, and even the repo's own README advises sourcing from the individual databases rather than scraping the portal. No open reuse/redistribution license for eChemPortal-served data could be located (the legal-notice page is a JavaScript SPA that did not yield its terms to automated fetch). Absent an explicit grant, and given the data is third-party-owned and would require separate per-source licenses, this is conservatively recorded as licenseClass 'unknown' (marker Lr) with commercial use 'prohibited' and dcterms:license unstated; substantively treat it as restricted (a separate per-source license would be required). HUMAN REVIEWER: confirm eChemPortal's terms of use / disclaimer directly at echemportal.org, and note that any redistribution would also need to respect each contributing database's own license (e.g. ECHA Legal Notice, EPA open data, Health Canada, OECD).",
  "dcterms:creator": "OECD and participating national/regional chemical authorities",
